## What Is Low Voltage Wiring?

Low voltage wiring carries 50 volts or less and powers the technology side of your building—think network cabling, cameras, speakers, and smart devices. It’s separate from your regular electrical wiring but just as important for reliable connectivity.

## What Is Low Voltage Wiring Used For?

It’s used for structured cabling, Wi-Fi access points, security systems, and automation controls. Planning these lines early keeps them hidden and ensures your systems work flawlessly for years.

[Learn more about low voltage cabling](https://brinkdesign.co/blog/low-voltage-wiring-explained-what-homeowners-and-builders-need-to-know)
